{"full":"hf:FlameF0X/cpu-lm-benchmark","spaceId":"FlameF0X/cpu-lm-benchmark","name":"CPU LM Speed Leaderboard","source":"huggingface","description":"Benchmark base LMs (10M–1B) on CPU — speed and quality","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","benchmark","leaderboard","small-language-models","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":9,"created":"2026-09-11T17:24:20.000Z","updated":"2026-09-12T14:53:03.000Z","license":"apache-2.0","runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://flamef0x-cpu-lm-benchmark.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/FlameF0X/cpu-lm-benchmark","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T21:22:28.278Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T21:22:28.278Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T21:22:28.278Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"⚡","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Enter any base causal language model on the Hub with between 10M and 1B parameters and this Space benchmarks it on CPU: it measures prefill speed (prompt tokens / second) AND decoding speed (generated tokens / second) at every rung of a prompt-length ladder — 64, 256, 1024, 4096 and 11264 tokens (median of 3 timed runs per length up to 1024, one warm-up run discarded; 2 timed runs without warm-up above 1024) — and measures perplexity on a fixed 20×512-token slice of the WikiText-2 raw test set as a quality score.","Results are stored as JSON in the public bucket FlameF0X/lm-cpu-benchmarks — one file per model — and the Leaderboard tab reads them all, with a filter by model size.","the entry check: detection uses the model card's basemodel metadata plus name patterns (instruct, chat, sft, dpo, …), and the leaderboard also hides already-stored entries that match. This board compares architectures' raw speed and coherence, not fine-tuning effort."],"features":["Base models only. Fine-tuned, instruct and chat models are rejected at","Between 10M and 1B parameters. Models under 10M are hidden from the"],"sourceUr